Alright, let's implement pov.go. The tests compare trees by value and children (allowing reordering of children), so FromPov can return a new tree or restructure in-place. The simplest approach: build a new tree by reparenting.

Implementation plan:

```go
package pov

type Tree struct {
	value    string
	children []*Tree
}

func New(value string, children ...*Tree) *Tree {
	return &Tree{value: value, children: children}
}

func (tr *Tree) Value() string { return tr.value }

func (tr *Tree) Children() []*Tree { return tr.children }
