```

Wait, this approach has a subtle issue: when recursing, if from is found in a subtree, the new subtree's root is the found node, and the parent becomes a child of the found node. But the parent node itself must be reconstructed with the found child removed. Let me think.

Better approach: build the whole new tree recursively:

```go
func (tr *Tree) fromPov(from string, parent *Tree) *Tree {
	if tr.value == from {
		children := append(append([]*Tree{}, tr.children...), parent)
		if parent == nil {
			children = tr.children  // or just the copy
		}
		return &Tree{value: tr.value, children: children}
	}
	children := make([]*Tree, 0, len(tr.children))
